/**
 * Bulk-import the real Vintage Story ModDB catalogue into `GameMod` — closes
 * a genuine zero-mod gap (`vintagestory` had no rows at all before this).
 * Same shape/safety rails as `scripts/import-modio-catalog.ts`; read that one
 * first if you haven't. This one only documents where Vintage Story's API
 * shape differs.
 *
 * SOURCE: `https://mods.vintagestory.at/api/mods` + `/api/mod/{urlalias}` —
 * the real, official Vintage Story ModDB API. Checked live 2026-09-24:
 * MIT-licensed (per the ModDB's own published terms), keyless, no rate-limit
 * documented. 8,684 mods confirmed live in the bulk list.
 *
 * ONE REQUEST GETS EVERYTHING (unlike every other importer in this repo):
 * `/api/mods` is NOT paginated — it returns all 8,684 mods' summary rows in a
 * single response (confirmed live: `{"statuscode":"200","mods":[...8684
 * entries...]}`, no `page`/`cursor`/`total` envelope at all). So this script
 * has no page-walking loop for the list step; the "pages" a normal importer
 * would burn through instead becomes one rate-limited detail call PER
 * QUALIFYING mod (see QUALITY THRESHOLD below for why that stays a bounded,
 * reasonable number rather than 8,684 calls).
 *
 * SERVER-RELEVANCE FILTER: Vintage Story's ModDB publishes a real `side`
 * field per mod — "client" | "server" | "both" — set by the mod's own
 * author, not inferred. Checked the live distribution across all 8,684 mods:
 * both=7,003, client=868, server=813. `side: "client"` is excluded outright
 * (868 mods, ~10% — cannot run on a dedicated server at all), matching this
 * repo's established principle (Modrinth's `environment` facet, mod.io Core
 * Keeper's "Application Type" tags) of only filtering where the source draws
 * a REAL client/server distinction — Vintage Story's `side` is exactly that,
 * author-set, not guessed.
 *
 * QUALITY THRESHOLD: downloads > 1000 (DEFAULT_MIN_DOWNLOADS, same floor as
 * Modrinth/mod.io). Checked live where this lands: 3,932 of the 7,816
 * server-relevant (both/server) mods clear it — top mods run 800k-1.16M
 * downloads (BetterRuins, Carry On, Primitive Survival), so this is a real,
 * meaningful cut, not a no-op or a catalogue-gutting one. Applied BEFORE the
 * per-mod detail fetch (see above) so this script makes ~3,932 detail calls,
 * not 8,684 — still bounded and reasonable at a conservative rate.
 *
 * FIELD NOTES (per-mod detail call, `/api/mod/{urlalias}`):
 *   - `description` = the list endpoint's own `summary` (short tagline,
 *     already available with zero extra calls).
 *   - `longDescription` = the detail endpoint's `text` — real author-written
